# Round 18, C1-14 (fixed). L §5.11 Ties are stated: over things, movements or an open index's keys, first and last
# "without [ties by] are refused, at load where load sees the binding (§8.4), otherwise at the key (RUN-TIE)"; a
# binding over a kind is seen at load. L §8.4: an order on things is refused "at load where the types show it
# (LOAD-UNIT, LOAD-DOMAIN)"; this interpreter gives it LOAD-UNIT, as for min over things. The refusal is the whole
# reality's (q, which needs no order, isn't printed). snap11: q2 RUN-TIE.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
kind persons
input age_of[p in persons]: int
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ola] lives 1950-01-01..
  persons + [jan] lives 1960-01-01..
  age_of[ola] = 70
  age_of[jan] = 60
ask q: count(p in persons on 2026-06-01)
ask q2: first(p in persons on 2026-06-01 where age_of[p] > 0)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT first over things has no ties by (m.tally:18)
